  "diagProxyGuidePrepareTitle": "1. Check the local proxy first",
  "diagProxyGuidePrepare": "Select a valid profile, start the connection in FlClash, and make sure Local proxy listener passes before entering the proxy address.\nQuit other proxy apps that may keep changing system settings. If your company or school manages the settings, or they are locked or keep reverting, check with the administrator.",
  "diagProxyGuideManualTitle": "2. Check or enter the proxy settings",
  "diagProxyGuideWindows": "Settings → Network & internet → Proxy\nIf automatic settings are left over from another app and your network no longer needs them, turn off Use setup script and Automatically detect settings.\nUnder Manual proxy setup, enable Use a proxy server, enter the address and port below in their separate fields, and save. Do not prefix the address with http://. Keep any exceptions your network needs.",
  "diagProxyGuideMacos": "System Settings → Network → active Wi-Fi or Ethernet service → Details → Proxies\nmacOS 12: System Preferences → Network → active service → Advanced → Proxies\nIf automatic settings are left over from another app and your network no longer needs them, turn off Auto proxy discovery and Automatic proxy configuration.\nEnable Web proxy (HTTP) and Secure web proxy (HTTPS). Enter the address and port below for both, then save. Keep any bypass entries your network needs.",
  "diagProxyGuideLinux": "Open your desktop settings → Network → Network Proxy and select Manual (names vary by desktop).\nEnter the address and port below for both HTTP and HTTPS, then apply. If there is no system proxy panel, configure the target app instead.\nBefore replacing an automatic configuration, check its source and whether your network still needs it.",
  "diagProxyGuideApp": "On this device, open the target app’s proxy settings, choose HTTP or SOCKS5, and enter the address and port below.\nAndroid provides the system proxy through the VPN service. For VPN access, check the VPN switch and app access control in FlClash network settings.",
  "diagProxyGuideAuthenticated": "Local proxy authentication is enabled, so FlClash does not apply a system proxy automatically.\nIn an app that supports proxy authentication, choose HTTP or SOCKS5 and enter the address and port below. Use the username and password from FlClash → Override → General → Inbound → Authentication.\nDo not include credentials in diagnostic reports.",
  "diagProxyGuideValues": "Local address: 127.0.0.1\nMixed port (current configuration): {port}\nUse this mixed port for HTTP, HTTPS website proxying, or SOCKS5 on this device only.",
  "diagProxyGuideInvalidPort": "The mixed port is unavailable. Set a valid port in Ports and authentication, then start the connection.",
